{
  "id": "GtaHospitalBillC02",
  "slug": "gta-hospital-bill/c02",
  "chapter": "The rules",
  "topic": "What if you got the GTA6 hospital bill in real life?",
  "script": [
    {
      "beat": "how it started",
      "text": "It starts on a Saturday morning, after a very long night with a controller in your hand. You trip on the stairs, and the world blinks grey. When it comes back, you're outside City General, three streets away, in your pyjamas. Perfectly fine. A nurse stares at you. Then your phone buzzes. Your first bill: two thousand, nine hundred and nine dollars, for falling down the stairs. You fall down a few more things that morning, on purpose this time. That's how you figure out the rules."
    },
    {
      "beat": "rule one",
      "text": "Rule one: you can't die. Whatever happens, you blink, and you're back at the hospital doors, healed."
    },
    {
      "beat": "rule two",
      "text": "Rule two: the bill is real. Every line is the real price of what just happened to you, at real American hospital prices, as if you had to recover the normal way. A broken leg gets billed like a broken leg, even if it heals in a blink."
    },
    {
      "beat": "rule three",
      "text": "Rule three: the bill only ever comes to you. Nobody else pays a cent."
    },
    {
      "beat": "the total",
      "text": "By ten in the morning, the number at the top of your phone says sixty-three thousand, three hundred and twenty dollars. You have eleven dollars in your bank account. And it's only Saturday."
    }
  ],
